SUMMARY:PETALUMA ART HATCHERY: Artist Open Studios
DESCRIPTION:ART HATCHERY OPEN STUDIO\nDATE: Saturday\, April 18 \, 2026\nTIME: 12 pm – 5 pm\nPLACE: Art Hatchery Studios\n401 7th street   ( between F & G streets)\nPetaluma\, Ca 94952 \nThe Art Hatchery is a diverse group of Petaluma artists working across painting\, photography\, fiber art\, printmaking\, and mixed media. This is not a gallery—it’s a living\, working studio environment where creativity happens every day. During Open Studios\, visitors can step inside\, meet the artists\, and discover original work in an authentic\, approachable setting.  \nThe Art Hatchery\, a historic brick chicken hatchery built in 1906\, has been converted into artist studios.  Artists in this collective include:  \nLance Kuehne: fine art photographer / https://lancekuehne.com/ \nSee See Lo: painter / https://www.botzilla.com/see_see_lo.html \nNancy Lloyd: oil painter / https://nancylloydart.com/ \nJoanne Tepper: oil painter / https://joannetepper.com/ \nAndrea E Leland: printmaker & painter / https://andrealeland.com/ \nMichele Rosett: painter / https://michelerosett.squarespace.com/ \nStephanie Sherratt: paper fabricator / https://www.instagram.com/paperfabricglitter/ \nHamish Hafter: framer / owner of Edge Gallery  \nElizabeth Pond McPherson: fiber sculpture / https://www.surfacedesign.org/author/artiquesme-com/ \nMargo Carroll: textile artist & quiltmaker \nPhyllis Calvin-Thomas: oil painter / https://www.phylliscalvinthomas.com/ \nJim Thomas: photographer / https://www.jimthomasphotography.com/
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/petaluma-art-hatchery-artist-open-studios/
LOCATION:Petaluma Art Hatchery\, 401 F Street\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art
END:VEVENT
