SUMMARY:The Musical Comedy Murders of 1940 at 6th Street Playhouse
DESCRIPTION:A team of Broadway creatives are hoping for a stroke of luck. With their recent Broadway disaster fresh in their memory\, they gather a group of singers\, dancers\, actors\, and a director for an important meeting in Westchester\, hoping to secure a wealthy backer for their next project. But tensions rise (and hilarity ensues) when the infamous “Stage Door Slasher” arrives\, leading the A-list team through a series of comic mishaps and pure murderous pandemonium. Will the artists discover the killer? Or will the “Stage Door Slasher” live to lurk another day?
